INSERT INTO feature VALUES('layout-as-model','layouts','A layout as a model of a theory','two-layouts-one-code','partial','uncommon','mainstream languages','A type is the terms of its theory, `Terms(S)`, and a layout of it is a module that models that theory, `Model(S)`, whose carrier is the terms of a second theory: the bits and their rules. The encoder is the fold into the layout. The decoder is a fold that respects the rules of the bits, through a model of the bits whose members prove each rule. The two round trips give an equivalence of the two types of terms, which `ua` makes a path between them: a truth value is laid out so in one bit of the `llvm` dialect, with the conjunction of two bits and its two rules. A layout that gives two constants one bit pattern is a model, and it is refused at its round trip. Where a rule of the type joins two constants, the layout gives them one bit pattern: the rule is a member of the layout that holds a path between the two patterns, and the encoder is a case that rests on that law. Each fold is written by hand (#4148, #4149): no derivation reads the theory value of the type, and no memory holds a bit yet.',NULL,'corpus/model/layouts/truth-in-one-bit.gandr corpus/pathological/layouts/truth-in-one-bit.gandr corpus/model/layouts/signal-in-one-wire.gandr','corpus/ledger/features/layout-as-model.gandr','#4148 #4149');
